Yes, I know the way to win nethack is to be careful and avoid stupid
mistakes, but I just lost *another* winning game because I miskeyed
and fell into the moat in the castle.

I was very prepared. I'd already trucked around the moat twice with my
boots of levitation. I had an AC-25, intrinsic teleport. I had 2 more
wishes on my wand of wishing, some scrolls of charging left. I was at
the point of gathering food, to go explore hell once w/o the amulet,
leaving breadcrumbs behind to feed me. This game was going to win.

I had even been extra patient, tracking up 15 dungeon levels just to
find a fountain to make some holy water. Hours in this game.

And it's all lost because I typed "6" instead of "3". This sucks.

Lots of other stupid death's give you a confirm prompt - why can't
pools?
